  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836968",
      "title": "Extracting Code & Improving Code Structure",
      "sourceHash": "120125d07ca2b4852a9d738f3d078e66adfa4fd40fb27b6b1dc96effe6bf7f4f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 2.58,
          "en": "Now to clean up the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.58,
          "end": 6.27,
          "en": "in this AvailablePlaces file a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.27,
          "end": 8.52,
          "en": "and make this file a bit leaner,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.52,
          "end": 11.64,
          "en": "I will now add a separate helper file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.64,
          "end": 16.64,
          "en": "which I'll name http.js next to the loc.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.13,
          "end": 19.5,
          "en": "which is totally optional,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.5,
          "end": 24.5,
          "en": "but where I wanna add a separate function, an async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.68,
          "end": 30.68,
          "en": "called fetchAvailablePlaces which should be exported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 33.09,
          "end": 38.09,
          "en": "And my idea is to place this data fetching code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 38.55,
          "end": 42.45,
          "en": "this code here in the end where we fetch the place data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 42.45,
          "end": 44.68,
          "en": "in this http.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 50.43,
          "en": "So I will grab this code here where I sent the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 50.43,
          "end": 55.29,
          "en": "and check whether it's okay and cut it from AvailablePlaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 55.29,
          "end": 58.083,
          "en": "and instead move it in here into fetchAvailablePlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 60.84,
          "end": 64.95,
          "en": "And then there after we checked that the response is correct",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 64.95,
          "end": 66.9,
          "en": "if we did not throw an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 66.9,
          "end": 70.653,
          "en": "I also wanna return resData.places here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 72.12,
          "end": 74.28,
          "en": "So that this is a utility function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 74.28,
          "end": 77.01,
          "en": "that can be called to send that request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 77.01,
          "end": 80.763,
          "en": "and either get back an error or the places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 82.74,
          "end": 87.74,
          "en": "And back in AvailablePlaces, I now will import this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 89.61,
          "end": 93.273,
          "en": "from this newly added http.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 94.28999999999999,
          "end": 97.053,
          "en": "and here I named the function fetchAvailablePlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 101.37,
          "end": 105.18,
          "en": "And we can now call this here, still in that try block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 105.18,
          "end": 109.83,
          "en": "because of course, fetchAvailablePlaces may throw an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 109.83,
          "end": 111.78,
          "en": "either because we throw it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 111.78,
          "end": 114.15299999999999,
          "en": "or because the fetch function throws one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 117.47999999999999,
          "end": 121.35,
          "en": "So we'll execute it here in the try block and still await it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 121.35,
          "end": 125.73,
          "en": "because fetchAvailablePlaces will return a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 125.73,
          "end": 127.83,
          "en": "because every function you decorate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 127.83,
          "end": 130.323,
          "en": "with async will yield a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 132.21,
          "end": 133.89,
          "en": "So here we can await this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 133.89,
          "end": 137.52,
          "en": "and we'll get back our places or an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 137.52,
          "end": 139.95,
          "en": "but now we can use the places here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 139.95,
          "end": 142.71,
          "en": "instead of resData.places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 142.71,
          "end": 145.8,
          "en": "And the rest of the code can therefore stay the way it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 145.8,
          "end": 150.8,
          "en": "But now we were able to outsource this actual fetching code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 151.07999999999998,
          "end": 155.13,
          "en": "the actual code that sends the HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 155.13,
          "end": 158.79,
          "en": "And we could now potentially reuse that in other places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 158.79,
          "end": 162.243,
          "en": "of the application that needs the same data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 164.13,
          "end": 166.77,
          "en": "And with that, if we save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 166.77,
          "end": 169.47,
          "en": "you will see that this should still work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 169.47,
          "end": 171.903,
          "en": "and we still fetch our places here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
